      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-2(x+13)^{2}+14?$",
      "worked_solution": "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-13$ and $k=14,$ the vertex is $(-13,14).$\n\n- Since $a=-2<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,14].$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14250418/assets/08b2ebf2fb3ecb8e02eed81d47e349dad22bde0d97e8920fabc75a8e2301da2b.png)",
